  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It builds a 260×260 ground plane and 10,000 instanced objects as three instanced draws. Typecheck passes, but I couldn't run `vite build` or the scene here, so it hasn't been rendered or checked in a browser. The draws are 8,000 trunks (cylinders), 8,000 canopies (cones) and 2,000 rocks (squashed spheres). Placement uses a seeded LCG (seed 20240607) over a 70-unit radius, so the forest is the same on every load. Canopies get per-instance HSL greens and rocks get per-instance greys and browns through the `colors` option on a white base material. The scene has one shadow-casting directional light, a hemisphere fill light and `effects.fog` in `exp` mode. The camera is `camera.orbit` with `autoRotate: 0.12`, placed so the whole forest is in view. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set two animation frames after `app.ready()` resolves, as an approximation of the first drawn frame. The engine runs its own render loop, so the file has no explicit `requestAnimationFrame` loop.",
